      "worked": "Take the inverse pair $f(x)=x^2$ with domain $(-\\infty,0]$ and $g(x)=-\\sqrt{x}$ with domain $[0,\\infty)$.\n\nAt $x=-1$,\n$$\\begin{align*}g(f(-1))&=-\\sqrt{(-1)^2}\\\\g(f(-1))&=-1.\\end{align*}$$\nHowever, $g(-1)$ is undefined, so $f(g(-1))$ is undefined. This is a domain failure, not two unequal defined values. For this pair both compositions are defined only at $x=0$, where they are equal.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
